why: BACKLOG "the original entry — OPEN, and now the PRIMARY lane":
  three quarters of the elementwise consumer's thread time is parked,
  and the diagnosis is one unpark per element once the producer
  saturates the ring. The entry says every number predates the chunked
  feed and must be re-taken on its own harness first. Plan: (1) before
  — ChannelGuaranteeBenchmark okaySentinelElem/okayStrongElem/
  okaySentinelChunk and ChannelGranularityBenchmark okayElementwise/
  okayChunked, -prof gc; (2) a probe counting wakeOne successes per
  element in okaySentinelElem (one side, a static counter is honest
  here: only the consumer wakes senders); (3) if the count is near one
  per element, a consumer-local policy: wake one sender every k-th pop
  and all senders before the consumer parks (liveness), no read of
  the producer's line per pop — hasRoom/size read `tail`; (4) A/B on
  the same lanes, laws TestChannelLaws + the cross channel suites.
